1
00:00:00,765 --> 00:00:01,975
Sheldon, I've got to ask.

2
00:00:02,133 --> 00:00:04,633
(Penny:)How did you figure out
that it was the geology lab?

3
00:00:04,803 --> 00:00:05,613
(Sheldon:)Oh, simple.

4
00:00:05,770 --> 00:00:08,720
The Arrah Arrah in the riddle
meant Jan Arrah,

5
00:00:08,873 --> 00:00:11,443
(Sheldon:)a member of the Legion of
Superheroes known as Element Lad.

6
00:00:11,610 --> 00:00:14,780
And then the word "He,"
it wasn't the masculine pronoun,

7
00:00:14,946 --> 00:00:17,616
but rather, "H-E,"
the abbreviation for helium.

8
00:00:17,649 --> 00:00:19,599
(Sheldon:)See where I'm going with this?

9
00:00:21,653 --> 00:00:24,493
(Howard:)-Yes.
-Nice try.

10
00:00:24,656 --> 00:00:26,826
(Sheldon:)Now, Element Lad's ability

11
00:00:26,992 --> 00:00:28,992
(Sheldon:)is the power to transmute
chemical elements.

12
00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:31,610
(Sheldon:)Helium has an atomic number of two.

13
00:00:31,763 --> 00:00:35,613
(Sheldon:)If you multiply that by the
atomic number of "N," nitrogen,

14
00:00:35,767 --> 00:00:40,077
(Sheldon:)you get 14, which is
the atomic number of...?

15
00:00:42,307 --> 00:00:45,687
(Sheldon:)I'm just funnin' you, silicon.
And that is the most common element

16
00:00:45,844 --> 00:00:47,954
(Sheldon:)in the Earth's surface.
So that narrowed it down

17
00:00:48,113 --> 00:00:50,023
(Sheldon:)to the geology lab
or the chemistry lab.

18
00:00:50,181 --> 00:00:52,421
(Howard:)Wow.

19
00:00:52,584 --> 00:00:54,824
(Penny:)I can drink a beer underwater.

20
00:00:56,021 --> 00:00:57,861
(Sheldon:)And I'm sure your parents are proud.

21
00:00:58,023 --> 00:01:02,373
(Sheldon:)Now, finally, the line
"in this room the thing you'll see"

